        comment     2026-11-23T04:00:01Z
            Slice state inventory (requirements lead, 2026-11-23): one owner function per state, decided once for the
            slice; transition tables are the Spec's, cited not restated.

            Each state: owner (Task); writers today -> after; what is saved.

            - Lane, displaced head: `cells.ts#table` via `lane-moves` (T121; table unchanged, I20); unchanged, and
              guards read it only through `lanes.viewOf`; saved as Records' head.
            - Owed row (+`input`, +`refusal`): `ledger.ts` (T121): `owe` (one unknown per Attempt), `afterTry` (Rows
              table: delivery x Heard/Unmapped/Refused), `letGo`, `suspend`, `start`, `restore`; ledger only, and
              `refusal` is written only by `afterTry`; `input` saved, `refusal` never.
            - Ending issue: no owner, `issuesOf` reads `Owed.refusal` (T121); today stored under `IssueSource.Operation`
              by name, deleted; never saved.
            - Read entry `entries[contract][keyText]`: `entries.ts#apply`, the entry table, total over cue x phase
              (T122); today none (`World.reads` per call), after: cues Ask Lookup/Refetch, Invalidate, Written, Clear,
              Settled, Last hold left, First hold arrives, Collect due, Install, Runtime ends; `data` and `at` saved
              when persist.
            - Read slot `slots[life][operation]`: `entry-slots.ts` (T122); lookup, refetch, cancel, freeze, end;
              never saved.
            - Placement (life, path): `entry-placements.ts` (T123): unplace at exit, freeze, end; place at entry, thaw;
              new; never saved.
            - Releasing call + `Alarm.Release`: `entry-releases.ts#release` adds and sets the alarm; `ended` (called by
              the dispatch) removes and clears it (T123); new, and the table's Release move calls `release` (crossing
              value: CallId); never saved.
            - `Alarm.Collect`: `entries.ts#unheld` sets it (Last hold left, Idle; Install), First hold arrives clears it
              (T122); the union holds it with no writer today; never saved.
            - Saved entry `entry/<contract>|<keyText>`: Records' Shape codec (kind, T124), written when data lands,
              deleted at Clear and Collect, kept at Runtime ends, deleted at install when too old or undecodable (T124);
              new; it is the save.
            - Services list on a Compiled operation: static, boot check `MissingService` (T121); new; n/a.
            - Deleted: `World.reads`, `IssueSource.Operation`, `CleanupOverdue` (T122, T121, T123).
            - Owners as built (building lead, 2026-11-23): `entries.ts#apply` counts live optimistic layers as holds;
              `entry-writes.ts` owns layers and success writes, through entries' put and apply; `entry-store.ts` owns
              saved entries and install (in-memory install is T48's); `read-rows.ts` derives the snapshot's read rows;
              `issues-of.ts` derives the issues. Lane heads' other writers remain T121's open item.

            Freeze and thaw: no life freezes in production before instances (T109), so the freeze cells of slots (T122)
            and placements (T123) are built as functions here and their Stories wait on T109.
