    T102
        title       Core shapes: typed reason codes, branded runtime ids, chain state, one turn cause
        status      done
        priority    medium
        description
            The core's reason codes, runtime ids, chain state and turn cause each become one typed shape, so the wrong
            combinations the current shapes allow can't be written.

            **Why now:** the idiom survey of 2026-11-19 (user's B) found four core shapes that work today but each
            permit a silent wrong behaviour on a later change (as at commit `8f156353`): `forget` drops held lanes only
            while a free-string reason equals `"operation"` (`record.ts` `OPERATION_GONE`); consumer start order is
            parsed back out of an incarnation id's text (`world.ts` `startOrder`); a chain id is `chains.size + 1` with
            a `0` sentinel, correct only while chains are cleared all at once (`tx.ts`); a turn's cause is three
            `Option`s plus a `source` that repeats them, with invalid mixes representable (`serve.ts` `turn`).

            **Read first:** code:packages/flow-state-v3/src/core/record.ts, code:packages/flow-state-v3/src/core/tx.ts,
            code:packages/flow-state-v3/src/core/serve.ts, @spec.Turn, @spec.Actors.R13 (the loop guard's chains).

            **Approach:** each item names its wrong ending first (the user's rule: every check prevents one), then red,
            then the shape:

            - reason and decline codes: one `Schema.Literals` set each, used by `Result.fail`, `quarantined` and
              `Guard.Check`; `retiredOperation` matches a member, not a string;
            - runtime ids: branded `IncarnationId`, `AttemptId`, `ChainId` from one mint; `Incarnation` stores `started`
              (the mint's counter), and no code parses an id;
            - chain state: `Following = Idle | Admitted | Chained` replaces the two `let`s; `Mail.chain`
              is `Option<ChainId>`;
            - turn cause: `Cause = Event | Firing | Ending`, with the own lane and the source derived.

            Out of scope: the ending triple, lane-record nullables, `~flow` probes and findings by mutation
            (trust-boundaries consult with @task.V3.T92 and @task.V3.T98); the edge's capture state and the mailbox
            (@task.V3.T99's lifetimes redesign); the root `""` path and per-slot maps (left for the convergence that
            next touches tree or slots). The raw-throw class stays in @task.V3.T98.

            May change: `packages/flow-state-v3/src/core/`, `tests/`, @spec.Turn and @spec.Actors with `specs.log`
            notes. Evidence: this Task's comments.

            False pass: a brand added in types while code still builds and parses ids as text → caught by a lint plant
            banning `.slice(`/`lastIndexOf` on id fields and a test that renames the mint's format.
        acceptance
            - Each of the four items has its wrong ending named and a check red before its change.
            - No core code compares a reason or decline code to a bare string, or parses an id's text.
            - Chain ids are minted; a partial clear of chains keeps every live chain's guard count (a test shows it).
            - `turn()` takes one tagged cause; the own lane and the issue source are derived from it.
            - A6: every branch over a closed set in the core is exhaustive (`$match` or a table keyed by tag), held by
              the `no-tag-chain` lint rule with plants.
            - A7: the bench worker rejects a malformed argument instead of reading it as a value.
            - A8: `owners-only` refuses an Exit read by value, `Effect.ignoreCause`, `Scope.close` and `??=`, planted.
            - `nub run check`, the suite and stress pass; `nub run faults --only` catches a planted fault per new check;
              the bench shows no regression on the turn hot path (`nub run bench --only <turn ids> --dev`).
        comment     2026-11-19T14:58:07Z
            [decided: agent lead 2026-11-19] One broad change: each fact the core branches on is born as a declared type
            (a literal catalogue, a branded minted id or a tagged enum) and each branch over it is a `$match` or a
            `satisfies Record<Tag, ...>` table. Why: per-item fixes each closed one trace and left siblings (isSaved,
            onWire, COMMITS, the Mail chain test) open. Reverse: per-site fixes. Guards: lint rules `no-tag-chain`,
            `no-id-text`; faults in code:packages/flow-state-v3/tests/typed-core-faults.ts; pins in
            code:packages/flow-state-v3/src/core/shapes.test.ts. Chains keep their own count so no pinned id shifts.
        comment     2026-11-19T14:58:08Z
            [decided: agent orchestrator 2026-11-19] Record decode and record-boundary brands (`AttemptId`, lane ids,
            key cuts in record.ts) stay with @task.V3.T92: `no-id-text` exempts record.ts with per-line reasoned
            disables. Also: A6 to A8 added to acceptance (small amendment); `Incarnation.started` is kept and live
            identities handled together go in start order. Why: reversing `byStart` swaps BlockedByDependents' message
            order and consumers' context turns. Reverse: derive order from the Map.
        comment     2026-11-19T14:58:09Z
            Traps: the worker-argv check was first red for the wrong reason (`turn.planted.none` is no bench, so the
            worker exits 0 on any argv; `--runs abc` hangs until killed), so use a real planted id with a passing
            control; a `@ts-expect-error` line needs a control line that must compile or any arity change satisfies it;
            `no-tag-chain` misses `[...].includes(x._tag)` and consecutive early-return `if`s, and `no-id-text` goes by
            name only (renamed bindings, `test`, `exec`, `charCodeAt`).
        comment     2026-11-19T14:58:10Z
            Still owed (routed to @task.V3.T105, unverified at compaction): an Actors rule for start order and a pin of
            `cartFirst` in `store.test.ts` so the fault `start-order-reversed` is caught; a pin or equivalence proof for
            mail between items (dropping `tx.followNone()` passes the suite); owners-only forms reading an Exit by value
