    T107
        title       Context slots: Flow.context on the definition, C.slot.change in the machine
        status      done
        priority    high
        blocked_by  [@T104]
        description
            Context slots are declared whole on the definition with `Flow.context` and read their one provider through
            typed tokens, and machines react with `C.slot.change({ when?, event })`, as the accepted proposal
            describes (@proposal.context-slots).

            **Why now:** a slot's `Provider.select(Schema, fn)` and a reaction's `select` are opaque functions over
            string keys: `when`'s arguments are `never`, a selector may read a field it should not, and the graph only
            knows "depends on all of the provider", so flow check, explain and graph cannot follow a context chain.

            **Read first:** @proposal.context-slots, code:packages/flow-state-v3/src/core/compiled.ts#Reaction,
            code:packages/flow-state-v3/src/core/compiled.ts#ContextSlot,
            code:packages/flow-state-v3/src/host/wiring.ts.

            **Risk:** the one-provider type ban needs a definition's `id` kept as its literal; @task.V3.T104's token
            brand (F3) provides it, so this Task follows T104. `onContext` inside a state node is built as an experiment
            beside the rest (accepted on condition, the user, 2026-11-20): it settles changes made while the state was
            inactive (silent baseline or one comparison on entry), and is kept only if its Stories and faults show it
            adds no bugs, otherwise rejected and recorded.

            **Approach:** fixtures first (Stories for the wrong endings below), then `M` tokens, `Flow.context` in both
            forms, `C` with `.change`, field-level edges in Compiled, skip-unchanged recomputation, then convert every
            `Provider.select` and `onContext` site and drop the old shapes.

            May change: `packages/flow-state-v3/src/`, `tests/`, `fixtures/`, `bench/`, `tools/flow-state-lint/`,
            `apps/docs/`, the Specs that state context. Evidence: this Task's comments.

            Fixtures: the catalog's context rows and its six context forms (@convention.fixture-catalog, "Context
            forms"), each a Story and an edge-value sample in the apps the catalog names (shop, git, transfers, sign-in,
            workspace); every existing `onContext` and `Provider.select` site converted in place.

            False pass: a type test that passes because a token became `any` → every type test is two-sided, enforced by
            `flow-state/paired-refusals`. Gates: the one-provider construction check and the skip-unchanged
            recomputation, each with its own planted fault in `tests/faults.ts`, caught by `nub run faults --only`.
            User's read: the state-scoped `onContext` verdict and its entry rule; any change to the saved reaction
            baseline (Actors R18), since it changes the record format that @task.V3.T56 versions.
        acceptance
            - Fixtures meet @convention.fixtures before any code, proved by its sidecar review; the catalog's context
              items are each marked built (with a Story id) or left (with the later Task).
            - Wrong endings pinned red first: a `reads` mixing two providers, a read of a `Flow.private` field, a
              `select` or `when` using the wrong type, and a `.change` on an undeclared slot each fail to compile
              (two-sided type tests); a mixed-provider slot built through a cast throws `InvalidConfiguration`, and a
              planted fault dropping that check is caught by `nub run faults --only`.
            - `Flow.context(token)` and `Flow.context(Schema, { reads, select })` work for memory fields, state tokens
              and `X.state`; a turn that changes none of a slot's reads runs no select (a Story or bench shows it).
            - `.change` has only `when(current, previous, { memory })` and `event`; a reaction whose event no state
              handles is a construction error.
            - Compiled holds each slot's provider fields and each reaction's slot, and an inspection test reads
              the edges.
            - No `Provider.select` or reaction `select` remains; `nub run check`, the suite, stress and `nub run
              docs:build` pass.
            - State-scoped `onContext`: either kept, with its entry rule chosen and pinned by Stories (a change while
              the state was inactive, then entry) and a planted fault, or rejected with the evidence noted on this Task
              and the proposal.
