        title       Fast tests again: the home-rooms stress sweep back under its bound
        status      draft
        priority    high
        parent      [@T136]

        description
            The `sweep-stress-land-0` shard runs under its bound again, by making schedule firings cheap or by a
            recorded re-measurement of the bound.

            **Why now:** the shard runs 193 s against its 164 s bound (measured at 41 s earlier); the tree before T57's
            last round already took 207 s. The profile points at schedule work and record writes on every firing in the
            home-rooms Stories. The Epic takes a Task to make the tests fast again before the next one.

            **Read first:** @task.V3.T57 (its last close note), code:packages/flow-state-v3/src/core/schedules.ts,
            @convention.bench. Spec: @spec.Host.R10, @spec.Host.I18, companion `wiki/specs/v3/Host.md`;
            @spec.Schedules.R17, @spec.Schedules.I18, companion `wiki/specs/v3/Schedules.md`.

            The linked Spec is pre-coding analysis: follow it as best-guess guidance for how to build, not a strict
            contract; it should help a lot. Where building shows it wrong, fix the Spec and log the change
            in `wiki/specs/specs.log`.

            **Supersedes:** none of its own; the cost falls with the replacements of @task.V3.T118 and @task.V3.T119,
            which it measures. Do not delete it before its replacement lands and the suite passes.

            May change: `packages/flow-state-v3/src/`, `tests/`, `fixtures/`, `bench/`. Evidence: this Task's comments.
