        description
            Types cross into the erased core at named functions (`door`, `slot`). `Compiled` carries the derived fields
            its hot paths read (`Node.chain`, `depth` and `leaf`, and `handledTags`), each written once by `indexOf` in
            one construction walk.

            **Why now:** split from @task.V3.T113 within the slice (the orchestrator's ruling, 2026-11-22). Its casts
            and scans are state of their own, apart from the face. The turn walk (@task.V3.T119) reads `Node.chain` and
            deletes `chainOf` and `leafOf`.

            **Read first:** @spec.Types.R7, @spec.Types.R13, @spec.Types.R14, @spec.Types.I4, @spec.Types.I10,
            @spec.Types.Q12, @spec.Types.Q15 and the Spec's Crossings, DerivedFields and ErasedCompiled sections,
            companion `wiki/specs/v3/Types.md`, and @task.V3.T113's comments (review blocker 1 and its ruling).

            **Build-time choice (`AnyBody`, @spec.Types.Q12, second spike):** assign `AnyBody` from every
            `MachineBody<D>`, with `on` handlers at `never`. If it compiles on the real package, `machine()`'s body
            decode returns the `AnyBody`, and the casts of `machine.ts` and `compile-body.ts#levelOf` go
            (`compile-schedules.ts` holds none). If it does not, those casts are handled at one point. Record the result
            as a decision tag with Why and Reverse.

            **Approach:**
            - The crossings `entry.ts#door` (absorbs `registered`, `trustedTokens`, `codecOf`, `trusted` and
              `Flow.context`'s overload cast) and `handles.ts#slot` (absorbs `erase`, `erasedWhen`, `trustedAttempt`).
            - The kind-brand casts in `definition.ts`, `machine.ts` and `send.ts`, and the same-class
              `handles.ts#member` and `handles.ts#guard`, fold into the `made.ts` doors.
            - The cast count is Types T7's ratchet, made exact (the orchestrator's ruling on the re-review,
              @task.V3.T142): T7 asserts `toBe(MOST)`, so each deletion lowers `MOST`, and at the close `MOST` is pinned
              to the measured count (at most 28: 39, less the 13 absorbed, plus `door` and `slot`). R13 counts each
              crossing as exactly 1 (an array, not a Set), and the counter counts every disable form naming the rule,
              not only `-next-line`. Beside `MOST`, the count in `src/host/testing/` (8 today) is pinned, since
              production imports it. The exact list of crossings, `host/snapshot.ts#project` and `snapshot.ts#asOutside`
              are @task.V3.T111's.
            - `indexOf` writes `Node.chain`, `depth` and `leaf`, and `Compiled.handledTags`, which replaces
              `machine.ts#handled` and is not a second computation. With `Node.leaf` written once, `Compiled.initial` is
              written once (today twice: `machine.ts:441` and `:481`).
            - The other derived fields go to their readers' Tasks (decision tag in @task.V3.T113's comments).
            - `compile-body.ts`: one accumulator walk with Map lookups.
            - Add the bench rows `construct.small`, `.wide` and `.deep`, and record check time per step (Q15). Bench
              runs are narrow `--only` runs.

            The linked Spec is pre-coding analysis: follow it as best-guess guidance for how to build, not a strict
            contract. Where building shows it wrong, fix the Spec and log the change in `wiki/specs/specs.log`.

            **Seams with @task.V3.T113:** `definition()`, whose face is T113's and whose kind-brand cast at its return
            is this Task's; and `machine()`, which reads T113's private config copy and returns the `AnyBody` this
            Task's spike decides.

